                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Scenario B (Technology and Performance): Average range is almost identical across battery types (about 324 to 326 km). Range depends more on vehicle category than on battery chemistry: Luxury Sedans and Luxury SUVs reach about 525 to 550 km, while Electric Buses and Trucks have the largest batteries (225 to 300 kWh) but only 226 to 270 km of range. Buses and trucks also charge at the highest power (about 340 to 350 kW), and scooters at the lowest.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Scenario C (Cost, Value and Sustainability): Average prices range from about $2,555 (Two-Wheeler Scooter) to about $274,543 (Electric Bus), yet customer ratings stay almost the same (4.08 to 4.10) and 3-year resale value stays at 52.7% to 54.2% in every segment. Family Daily Use saves the most CO2 (about 1.88 billion tons, roughly 42% of the 4.49 billion total).</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
